# Python Preferences

## Formatting

- When generating Python code, use Black formatting at all times.
    - This includes editing existing files which may not adhere to Black; new code must be compliant with Black.

## Docstring Style

- When creating docstrings, use Numpy-syle docstrings. Do not bother with a "Returns" section if the function does not return anything.

## Typehints

- Always use typehints in arguments, declariation, and import types from the typing library. Typehints also apply to return types.